#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:5
#: 48b9d05133704c138439287d0edb80bc
msgid "Thrust Loss and Yaw Imbalance Warnings"
msgstr "推力损失与偏航不平衡警告"

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:7
#: 93237f8bb6a84641b73ee564b28c6f8f
msgid ""
"If you see thrust loss or yaw imbalance warnings this page outlines some "
"checks and modifications that should be done to resolve the issue. In the "
"majority of cases these warnings are the result of incorrect hardware "
"selection or setup."
msgstr "如果您看到推力损失或偏航不平衡警告，本页概述了一些应执行的检查和修改以解决问题。在大多数情况下，这些警告是由于硬件选择或安装不正确所致。"

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:9
#: 8b4655b793014598a06792137dd94f14
msgid ""
"These warnings are designed to detect hardware failures in the propulsion "
"system. If they begin to occur on a vehicle that has been flying without "
"warnings the propulsion system should be checked. Warnings are more likely "
"to occur with larger payloads and in strong/gusty winds."
msgstr ""
"这些警告旨在检测推进系统中的硬件故障。如果之前飞行正常的飞行器开始出现此类警告，应检查推进系统。在负载较大和强风/阵风条件下，更容易出现警告。"

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:13
#: 4534273c4c6d4aa68026b7b92a636ccd
msgid "Potential Thrust Loss"
msgstr "潜在推力损失"

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:15
#: a872ece22bb24b3098f35976c9a2fb43
msgid ""
"If potential thrust loss messages are seen either on GCS or in the data-"
"flash logs, then an investigation should be done to find the cause and "
"remedy. The warning will give a motor number, for example:"
msgstr "如果在地面站或 dataflash 日志中看到潜在推力损失消息，应进行调查以找出原因并加以解决。警告将给出电机编号，例如："

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:17
#: 9509b0a1117d46a5ba9a3e91f5bc52f9
msgid "```Potential Thrust Loss (3)```"
msgstr "```Potential Thrust Loss (3)```"

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:19
#: 2f5b1ded9a754acda0d1774e7a83b6c1
msgid ""
"These warnings are the result of a motor or motors saturating at 100% "
"throttle. Because of this saturation ArduCopter can no longer achieve the "
"requested roll, pitch, yaw and throttle output. If this continues for a "
"prolonged period of time the vehicle will have reduced altitude and attitude"
" control and may crash."
msgstr ""
"这些警告是由于某个或某些电机在 100% 油门时饱和所致。由于这种饱和，ArduCopter "
"无法再实现所请求的横滚、俯仰、偏航和油门输出。如果这种情况持续较长时间，飞行器将失去高度和姿态控制，可能发生坠机。"

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:22
#: 66764eaeb7f64b40bb3c633fcc1ac4d1
msgid ""
"If these messages are seen in hover or relaxed flight, the problem must be "
"fixed in hardware. The vehicle's thrust to weight ratio should be increased,"
" either by a change in propulsion or reduction in mass."
msgstr "如果在悬停或平稳飞行时出现这些消息，必须通过硬件来解决问题。应提高飞行器的推重比，可以通过更换推进系统或减轻重量来实现。"

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:24
#: a70c8230685843ee9654895c9d24b31b
msgid ""
"If only seen in climbing and aggressive maneuvers it may be sufficient to "
"lower the requested accelerations and speeds. Again the vehicle's thrust to "
"weight ratio can be increased to allow higher accelerations and speeds."
msgstr "如果仅在爬升和剧烈机动时出现，可能只需降低请求的加速度和速度即可。同样，可以提高飞行器的推重比以允许更高的加速度和速度。"

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:29
#: a86f18c5dd82431abc6a03f7fff56a3b
msgid "Yaw Imbalance"
msgstr "偏航不平衡"

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:31
#: 989b377d52cb4006994d759dd3f2c29c
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The yaw imbalance warning is a measure of how hard the vehicle is working to"
" yaw, the warning will trigger before the yaw output is saturated. If the "
"yaw output becomes saturated the vehicle's ability to maintain yaw will be "
"compromised. And, in the worst case, this will result in the vehicle rapidly"
" spinning. The warning message gives a percentage of maximum yaw output. At "
"100% it is saturated. For example:"
msgstr ""
"偏航不平衡警告是衡量飞行器为维持偏航所付出努力的指标，该警告会在偏航输出饱和之前触发。如果偏航输出饱和，飞行器维持偏航的能力将受到损害。在最坏的情况下，这将导致飞行器快速旋转。警告消息给出最大偏航输出的百分比，100%"
" 时表示已饱和。例如："

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:34
#: 30869760b2904659937f418c1240de6a
msgid "```Yaw Imbalance 87%```"
msgstr "```Yaw Imbalance 87%```"

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:36
#: 46010cef17c942f098ce7d82e390474f
msgid ""
"If seen in hover, the issue should be resolved in hardware. If the value is "
"increasing with no pilot yaw input, the vehicle should be landed "
"immediately. Yaw imbalance can be recognized in dataflash logs by comparing "
"the PWM outputs between pars of opposing motors. It will present as a large "
"throttle level difference between the clockwise and counter clockwise "
"motors, as shown below:"
msgstr ""
"如果在悬停时出现，应通过硬件解决问题。如果该值在没有飞手偏航输入的情况下持续增大，应立即降落。偏航不平衡可以通过比较成对的反向电机的 PWM 输出在 "
"dataflash 日志中识别。它表现为顺时针和逆时针电机之间的较大油门差异，如下图所示："

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:42
#: 8615a607129741c2ba35ba289bea94f9
msgid ""
"This should be fixed in hardware. The most common cause is the motors not "
"being vertical on a circular arm. If the imbalance still persists the motors"
" can be tilted slightly such that the thrust angle assists the yaw for its "
"rotation direction. Some vehicles can be extremely sensitive to motors "
"thrust vector."
msgstr ""
"应通过硬件修复此问题。最常见的原因是电机在圆形臂上未垂直安装。如果不平衡仍然存在，可以稍微倾斜电机，使推力方向有助于其旋转方向的偏航。某些飞行器对电机推力矢量极为敏感。"

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:45
#: 74461a718ea148d98ffe54838a1c4565
msgid ""
"If the warning is only seen in aggressive yaw maneuvers, the warning "
"threshold can be increased by raising "
":ref:`ATC_RAT_YAW_IMAX<ATC_RAT_YAW_IMAX__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`.  "
"However, it may also be worth revisiting the yaw tune."
msgstr ""
"如果警告仅在剧烈偏航机动时出现，可以通过提高 "
":ref:`ATC_RAT_YAW_IMAX<ATC_RAT_YAW_IMAX__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>` "
"来增大警告阈值。但同时也值得重新审视偏航调参。"

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:48
#: 4c4f3cf44eef4b9c8731573733463a51
msgid ""
"Both the thrust loss and yaw imbalance warnings can be disabled with the "
":ref:`FLIGHT_OPTIONS<FLIGHT_OPTIONS>` parameter. This should only be done "
"after extensive log review and testing to verify the warnings are not "
"picking up genuine issues."
msgstr ""
"推力损失和偏航不平衡警告均可通过 :ref:`FLIGHT_OPTIONS<FLIGHT_OPTIONS>` "
"参数禁用。只有在经过大量日志审查和测试以确认警告不是针对真实问题后，才应这样做。"
